From: thongass000 <tienthong2004@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 00:53:45 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] EpdgService: Do not require Samsung's Wi-Fi Calling app

WfcActivityController.IsAvaliableWfcActivity() keeps the ePDG off unless
Samsung's Wi-Fi Calling app (com.sec.unifiedwfc) is installed. On AOSP
the Wi-Fi Calling switch is the framework's own, so count a missing app
as available; a disabled one still turns the ePDG off.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 smali/com/sec/epdg/WfcActivityController.smali | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/smali/com/sec/epdg/WfcActivityController.smali b/smali/com/sec/epdg/WfcActivityController.smali
index 9135c3d..6bc42ce 100644
--- a/smali/com/sec/epdg/WfcActivityController.smali
+++ b/smali/com/sec/epdg/WfcActivityController.smali
@@ -165,6 +165,8 @@
     :catch_0
     move-exception v3
 
+    const/4 v0, 0x1
+
     .line 50
     .local v3, "ie":Ljava/lang/IllegalArgumentException;
     new-instance v4, Ljava/lang/StringBuilder;
